I agree. I'd like to see spells modified pretty radically in conjunction with
more diverse characters: spells should be the primary weapon for wizards and
important for priests, although not necessarily the same spells. I think that
wizards should be discouraged from using heavy armor/weaponry with lousy 
combat abilities and penalties to spell use resulting from them. Instead, they
would have to have better defensive spells (e.g. the AD&D spells Globe of 
Invulnerability, elemental resistances, Force Shield, Wall of Force/Fire/Stone
etc.). I think that NH's biggest weakness is in the generic advanced chars.
An arch-mage should look and act differently from a high-level barbarian.

